cta_title: Broken Down in Sheffield Right Now?
===BODY===
          <h2>Steep streets</h2>
          <p>Some of Sheffield's residential streets are among the steepest in England, particularly in areas like Crookes, Walkley and Meersbrook. A car that's broken down on a hill needs care. Leave it in gear (or Park), with the handbrake on firmly and the wheels turned to the kerb, and tell us about the gradient and whether the car is likely to roll. That way the right recovery vehicle turns up.</p>

          <h2>The Parkway, the ring road and Meadowhall</h2>
          <p>The Sheffield Parkway links the city centre with the M1, and the inner ring road loops around the centre with busy junctions and tram crossings. Meadowhall, near the Tinsley Viaduct, draws huge traffic, especially at weekends. If you break down on one of these roads, get yourself somewhere safe first and tell us the road and nearest junction.</p>

          <h2>The M1 and the Tinsley Viaduct</h2>
          <p>The <a href="{{R}}routes/m1.html">M1</a> runs along the north-east edge of the city, crossing the Don valley on the double-deck Tinsley Viaduct at junction 34. It's elevated, busy and has little room to stop. If your car starts to struggle here, try to reach the next junction. If you can't, get as far left as you can, put your hazards on and wait behind the barrier if it's safe.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Driving a van?</strong> Sheffield has a Clean Air Zone around the inner ring road. Private cars aren't charged, but older non-compliant vans, taxis and lorries are. Tell us where your van needs to go and we'll plan around it.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Around Sheffield</h2>
          <p>We cover the whole city and South Yorkshire, including Rotherham, Barnsley, Doncaster and Chesterfield, and the edge of the Peak District. If you've broken down on a moorland road out towards the Peaks, tell us the road number and the nearest village.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: My car has broken down on a steep hill. Can you still recover it?
A: Yes. Recovery on hills is routine in Sheffield. Tell us how steep the street is and whether the car rolls, so we bring the right equipment.
Q: Does the Sheffield Clean Air Zone affect my car?
A: Private cars aren't charged in the Sheffield Clean Air Zone. Older non-compliant vans, taxis and lorries are. It doesn't affect recovering your vehicle.
Q: Do you cover Rotherham and Barnsley as well?
A: Yes. We arrange recovery across South Yorkshire, and we'll give you an honest arrival estimate when you call.
